[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'search query lasted about 0.21 seconds, and the search cost in the same test was about $9 per 1,000 tasks. Today I want to run some real-world tests and see exactly how it works. In a'

[00:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'broad search, I would'

[00:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'enter the following query: Find the most important AI agent platforms launched or significantly updated in the last 7 days. Check each release against the original sources, compare their architecture, tool integrations, pricing, and'

[00:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'deployment options , and provide me with the original links. This is a deliberately difficult question. To answer it properly, you need to research several different topics. Broad search breaks the main query into several'

[01:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'smaller queries and executes them in parallel. So instead of the agent performing the search in turn, several different paths are explored simultaneously, and eventually the relevant sources are gathered together. This is very'

[01:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'important for a research agent because as the number of search queries increases, their sequential execution can significantly increase the overall latency of the workflow. Now I\'ll move on to web search. Here I will enter a more direct query: Nvidia\'s latest announcements in the field of AI.'

[01:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Web search gives you more precise control over data retrieval. For example, the quantity parameter determines how many results will be returned. For a quick answer, a few results may be enough, but for a broader study, I may increase this number. Using the'

[01:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'search settings, I can also change the search type. And with domain filters, I can limit my search to only the sites I need or exclude certain domains entirely. For example, if I only need official Nvidia announcements, I can limit'

[01:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the results to official sources . The date range is also very useful when you are looking for recent information. If I search for news from this week, there\'s no reason for older results to fall into context. And if the title and'

[02:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'snippet are n\'t enough for the agent, I can enable full content so that the entire page text is also included in the output. On the right side, Octane also prepares the exact same request for Python, JavaScript, and curl. So everything I test here'

[02:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'can then be used directly in your own application or agent. Artificial Analysis measured Octane\'s speed at about 0.21 seconds per query , which was the best in that ranking. Now I\'m moving from'

[02:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'text search to another. In image search, I can upload an image and use it itself to find related content on the web . For example, if I have a photo of a product, location, or design, Octane can find related images'

[02:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and sources for them. Alongside this is video search, which does the same for video content and finds similar videos online. Image and video search is currently available in early access. Search APIs that combine'

[02:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'text, image, and video retrieval in a single stack for AI agents are still rare, and Octane is clearly expanding in this direction. The next section is multimodal chat. Multimodal chat'

[03:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'combines image understanding with web search. You can upload an image, ask a question about what\'s in it, and the system will find relevant information online, providing original sources. So, unlike a'

[03:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'conventional visual model that relies on existing knowledge, search becomes part of the workflow, bringing in fresh data. Next I move on to the model gateway. Here,'

[03:35] [scene:talk]
